    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS** with 68 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner resource.\n\n**Spec:** `ownerSegment` is `<TIER>_<AREA>` \u2014 TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel \u2265 3` else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when the locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` read-only string field (enum: `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) to the Owner schema, which generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` and two helper methods: `ownerSegment(Owner)` (derives from `membershipLevel(owner)` + `locality(owner)`) and `ownerSegment(int, String)` (derives from a supplied level/locality; METRO check uses `REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey`, whose keys are exactly NSW/VIC/QLD).\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 these responders already override `membershipLevel` with the household-capped value, so I recompute `ownerSegment` from that same capped level to keep the returned payload internally consistent.\n\nThe two new Cp55 tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and no existing test regressed.",
